rashes","c":"Optimizing database queries","d":"Using pointers to access heap memory"},{"q":"Which area of memory is used for dynamic memory allocation (e.g., malloc in C, new in C++)?","a":"Stack","b":"Heap","c":"Register","d":"Static Code Segment"},{"q":"Which tool allows developers to track and manage changes to source code over time?","a":"IDE","b":"Compiler","c":"Version Control System (e.g. Git)","d":"Debugger"},{"q":"Which SDLC model is characterized by sequential, non-overlapping phases? (HTML5 new features Focus)","a":"Waterfall Model","b":"Agile Model","c":"Scrum Model","d":"Spiral Model"},{"q":"What testing level focuses on testing individual modules or functions in isolation?","a":"Integration Testing","b":"System Testing","c":"Unit Testing","d":"Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"Which testing type evaluates code structure, logic paths, and internal execution paths?","a":"Black Box Testing","b":"White Box Testing","c":"Gray Box Testing","d":"User Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"What is ransomware?","a":"A virus that copies email addresses","b":"Malware that encrypts files and demands payment to restore access","c":"Adware that redirects search engines","d":"A tool used to scan network ports"},{"q":"Which cryptographic method uses public and private keys for encryption and decryption?","a":"Symmetric Encryption","b":"Asymmetric Encryption","c":"Hashing","d":"Salting"},{"q":"What technology maintains a decentralized, immutable ledger of transactions? (HTML5 new features Focus)","a":"Artificial Intelligence","b":"Cloud Computing","c":"Blockchain","d":"Internet of Things"},{"q":"What is a recommended strategy to manage time during an exam?","a":"Spend the first half of the time on the hardest question","b":"Answer easy questions first to build confidence and secure quick marks","c":"Do not read the instructions","d":"Leave early without reviewing answers"},{"q":"In exams with negative marking, what is the best approach when you have no idea about the answer?","a":"Guess 