s an SSD faster than a traditional HDD?","a":"It uses magnetic disks","b":"It has no moving mechanical parts and uses flash memory","c":"It is directly connected to the power supply","d":"It uses read/write optical lasers"},{"q":"What is the primary function of the BIOS?","a":"To manage user logins","b":"To perform the Power-On Self-Test (POST) and initialize system hardware","c":"To route internet traffic","d":"To compress hard drive data"},{"q":"Which protocol is responsible for transferring web pages from a server to a browser?","a":"FTP","b":"SMTP","c":"HTTP","d":"SSH"},{"q":"What does DNS stand for? (Data types Focus)","a":"Domain Name System","b":"Data Network Service","c":"Digital Name Server","d":"Dynamic Node System"},{"q":"Which HTTP status code represents a successful resource retrieval?","a":"200 OK","b":"301 Moved Permanently","c":"404 Not Found","d":"500 Internal Server Error"},{"q":"Which protocol is used to securely encrypt the connection between a browser and a server?","a":"HTTP","b":"FTP","c":"SSL/TLS (HTTPS)","d":"Telnet"},{"q":"What is the primary difference between IPv4 and IPv6?","a":"IPv4 is 128-bit, IPv6 is 32-bit","b":"IPv4 is 32-bit, IPv6 is 128-bit","c":"IPv4 uses letters, IPv6 uses only numbers","d":"IPv4 is secure, IPv6 is not secure"},{"q":"What is the worst-case time complexity of a Binary Search algorithm?","a":"O(1)","b":"O(n)","c":"O(log n)","d":"O(n log n)"},{"q":"What notation is used to describe the upper bound of an algorithm''s execution time? (Data types Focus)","a":"Omega Notation","b":"Theta Notation","c":"Big O Notation","d":"Alpha Notation"},{"q":"Which sorting algorithm splits an array in half, recursively sorts them, and merges them back?","a":"Bubble Sort","b":"Quick Sort","c":"Merge Sort","d":"Selection Sort"},{"q":"Which data structure follows the Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) access principle?","a":"Queue","b":"Stack","c":"Linked List","d":"Binary Tree"},{"q":"What is a major advantage of a Hash Table?","a":"It sorts elements automatically","b":"It provides average O(1) time complexity for search, insert, and delete operations","c":"It uses minimal memory","d":"It supports parent-child node relationships"},{"q":"Which OOP principle allows a class to inherit attributes and methods from another class?","a":"Encapsulation","b":"Inheritance","c":"Polymorphism","d":"Abstraction"},{"q":"What is Polymorphism? (Data types Focus)","a":"The ability of an object to take on multiple forms","b":"Hiding internal details using private attributes","c":"Bundling data and methods into a single class","d":"Running code in multiple threads"},{"q":"In OOP, what special function is automatically called when an object is instantiated?","a":"Destructor","b":"Constructor","c":"Getter","d":"Static method"},{"q":"What is exception handling?","a":"Finding syntax errors during compilation","b":"Managing runtime errors to prevent application crashes","c":"Optimizing database queries","d":"Using pointers to access heap memory"},{"q":"Which area of memory is used for dynamic memory allocation (e.g., malloc in C, new in C++)?","a":"Stack","b":"Heap","c":"Register","d":"Static Code Segment"},{"q":"Which tool allows developers to track and manage changes to source code over time?","a":"IDE","b":"Compiler","c":"Version Control System (e.g. Git)","d":"Debugger"},{"q":"Which SDLC model is characterized by sequential, non-overlapping phases? (Data types Focus)","a":"Waterfall Model","b":"Agile Model","c":"Scrum Model","d":"Spiral Model"},{"q":"What testing level focuses on testing individual modules or functions in isolation?","a":"Integration Testing","b":"System Testing","c":"Unit Testing","d":"Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"Which testing type evaluates code structure, logic paths, and internal execution paths?","a":"Black Box Testing","b":"White Box Testing","c":"Gray Box Testing","d":"User Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"What is ransomware?","a":"A virus that copies email addresses","b":"Malware that encrypts files and demands payment to restore access","c":"Adware that redirects search engines","d":"A tool used to scan network ports"},{"q":"Which cryptographic method uses public and private keys for encryption and decryption?","a":"Symmetric Encryption","b":"Asymmetric Encryption","c":"Hashing","d":"Salting"},{"q":"What technology maintains a decentralized, immutable ledger of transactions? (Data types Focus)","a":"Artificial Intelligence","b":"Cloud Computing","c":"Blockchain","d":"Internet of Things"},{"q":"What is a recommended strategy to manage time during an exam?","a":"Spend the first half of the time on the hardest question","b":"Answer easy questions first to build confidence and secure quick marks","c":"Do not read the instructions","d":"Leave early without reviewing answers"},{"q":"In exams with negative marking, what is the best approach when you have no idea about the answer?","a":"Guess randomly on all questions","b":"Skip the question entirely to avoid penalty points","c":"Always choose option C","d":"Mark two options"},{"q":"Convert the binary number 1011 to decimal:","a":"9","b":"11","c":"13","d":"15"},{"q":"What is the decimal equivalent of the Hexadecimal number ''A''?","a":"10","b":"11","c":"12","d":"15"}]',
  '{"ka":["b","a","b","b","b","b","a","b","b","b","b","a","b","b","c","a","a","c","b","c","c","c","b","b","b","a","b","b","b","c","a","c","b","b","b","c","b","b","b","a"]}',
  '["Inheritance allows a subclass to reuse code and behaviors defined in a parent superclass.","Polymorphism allows a single interface or method to represent different underlying forms (e.g. method overriding).","Constructors initialize newly created objects and are called automatically upon instantiation.","Exception handling (try-catch) intercepts errors at runtime, allowing graceful recovery.","The Heap is a large, unstructured pool of memory used for variables allocated dynamically at runtime.","1011 in binary is (1*8) + (0*4) + (1*2) + (1*1) = 11.","In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15.","The Octal number system uses eight digits (0-7) and has base 8.","First-generation computers (1940-1956) used vacuum tubes for circuitry and magnetic drums for memory.","The ALU performs arithmetic calculations (addition, subtraction) and logical decisions.","The Program Counter (PC) stores the address of the next instruction in sequence to be executed.","L1 cache is the fastest and closest to the CPU core, built directly on-die.","Solid State Drives (SSDs) read and write data electronically to flash memory, avoiding mechanical latency.","The BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) initializes hardware components and boots the system bootstrap loader.","Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is the foundation of data communication on the World Wide Web.","DNS stands for Domain Name System. It resolves domain names to numerical IP addresses.","The HTTP 200 OK status code indicates that the request has succeeded.","SSL/TLS encrypts HTTP communications, rendering them secure under HTTPS.","IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses, whereas IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses, providing a massive address space.","Binary search cuts the search space in half with each iteration, giving logarithmic time complexity O(log n).","Big O notation describes the worst-case time complexity, providing an asymptotic upper bound.","Merge Sort is a divide-and-conquer algorithm with a guaranteed worst-case time complexity of O(n log n).","A Stack utilizes LIFO operations. Elements are added (pushed) and removed (popped) from the top.","Hash tables store key-value pairs using a hash function, allowing constant-time access on average.","Inheritance allows a subclass to reuse code and behaviors defined in a parent superclass.","Polymorphism allows a single interface or method to represent different underlying forms (e.g. method overriding).","Constructors initialize newly created objects and are called automatically upon instantiation.","Exception handling (try-catch) intercepts errors at runtime, allowing graceful recovery.","The Heap is a large, unstructured pool of memory used for variables allocated dynamically at runtime.","Version Control Systems like Git track edits, support branching, and coordinate collaboration.","The Waterfall model is a rigid, step-by-step process where each phase must complete before the next begins.","Unit testing validates that small, isolated blocks of code (units) perform correctly.","White Box testing focuses on internal structures and requires access to the source code.","Ransomware locks or encrypts data, threatening to publish or delete it unless a ransom is paid.","Asymmetric encryption uses a public key to encrypt and a separate private key to decrypt.","Blockchain links cryptographic blocks in a distributed P2P consensus, guaranteeing immutability.","Securing easy points early ensures you don''''t run out of time for questions you definitely know.","Skipping questions you cannot eliminate options for prevents losing penalty points from negative marking.","1011 in binary is (1*8) + (0*4) + (1*2) + (1*1) = 11.","In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15."]',
  'published',
  datetime('now', '+360 hours')
);

