encrypt the connection between a browser and a server?","a":"HTTP","b":"FTP","c":"SSL/TLS (HTTPS)","d":"Telnet"},{"q":"What is the primary difference between IPv4 and IPv6?","a":"IPv4 is 128-bit, IPv6 is 32-bit","b":"IPv4 is 32-bit, IPv6 is 128-bit","c":"IPv4 uses letters, IPv6 uses only numbers","d":"IPv4 is secure, IPv6 is not secure"},{"q":"What is the worst-case time complexity of a Binary Search algorithm?","a":"O(1)","b":"O(n)","c":"O(log n)","d":"O(n log n)"},{"q":"What notation is used to describe the upper bound of an algorithm''s execution time? (Syntax error Focus)","a":"Omega Notation","b":"Theta Notation","c":"Big O Notation","d":"Alpha Notation"},{"q":"Which sorting algorithm splits an array in half, recursively sorts them, and merges them back?","a":"Bubble Sort","b":"Quick Sort","c":"Merge Sort","d":"Selection Sort"},{"q":"Which data structure follows the Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) access principle?","a":"Queue","b":"Stack","c":"Linked List","d":"Binary Tree"},{"q":"What is a major advantage of a Hash Table?","a":"It sorts elements automatically","b":"It provides average O(1) time complexity for search, insert, and delete operations","c":"It uses minimal memory","d":"It supports parent-child node relationships"},{"q":"Which OOP principle allows a class to inherit attributes and methods from another class?","a":"Encapsulation","b":"Inheritance","c":"Polymorphism","d":"Abstraction"},{"q":"What is Polymorphism? (Syntax error Focus)","a":"The ability of an object to take on multiple forms","b":"Hiding internal details using private attributes","c":"Bundling data and methods into a single class","d":"Running code in multiple threads"},{"q":"In OOP, what special function is automatically called when an object is instantiated?","a":"Destructor","b":"Constructor","c":"Getter","d":"Static method"},{"q":"What is exception handling?","a":"Finding syntax errors during compilation","b":"Managing runtime errors to prevent application crashes","c":"Optimizing database queries","d":"Using pointers to access heap memory"},{"q":"Which area of memory is used for dynamic memory allocation (e.g., malloc in C, new in C++)?","a":"Stack","b":"Heap","c":"Register","d":"Static Code Segment"},{"q":"Which tool allows developers to track and manage changes to source code over time?","a":"IDE","b":"Compiler","c":"Version Control System (e.g. Git)","d":"Debugger"},{"q":"Which SDLC model is characterized by sequential, non-overlapping phases? (Syntax error Focus)","a":"Waterfall Model","b":"Agile Model","c":"Scrum Model","d":"Spiral Model"},{"q":"What testing level focuses on testing individual modules or functions in isolation?","a":"Integration Testing","b":"System Testing","c":"Unit Testing","d":"Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"Which testing type evaluates code structure, logic paths, and internal execution paths?","a":"Black Box Testing","b":"White Box Testing","c":"Gray Box Testing","d":"User Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"What is ransomware?","a":"A virus that copies email addresses","b":"Malware that encrypts files and demands payment to restore access","c":"Adware that redirects search engines","d":"A tool used to scan network ports"},{"q":"Which cryptographic method uses public and private keys for encryption and decryption?","a":"Symmetric Encryption","b":"Asymmetric Encryption","c":"Hashing","d":"Salting"},{"q":"What technology maintains a decentralized, immutable ledger of transactions? (Syntax error Focus)","a":"Artificial Intelligence","b":"Cloud Computing","c":"Blockchain","d":"Internet of Things"},{"q":"What is a recommended strategy to manage time during an exam?","a":"Spend the first half of the time on the hardest question","b":"Answer easy questions first to build confidence and secure quick marks","c":"Do not read the instructions","d":"Leave early without reviewing answers"},{"q":"In exams with negative marking, what is the best approach when you have no idea about the answer?","a":"Guess randomly on all questions","b":"Skip the question entirely to avoid penalty points","c":"Always choose option C","d":"Mark two options"},{"q":"Convert the binary number 1011 to decimal:","a":"9","b":"11","c":"13","d":"15"},{"q":"What is the decimal equivalent of the Hexadecimal number ''A''?","a":"10","b":"11","c":"12","d":"15"},{"q":"Which number system uses base 8? (Syntax error Focus)","a":"Binary","b":"Octal","c":"Decimal","d":"Hexadecimal"},{"q":"Which electronic components characterized the first generation of computers?","a":"Transistors","b":"Vacuum Tubes","c":"Integrated Circuits (ICs)","d":"Microprocessors"},{"q":"What CPU component performs arithmetic and logical operations?","a":"Control Unit (CU)","b":"Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)","c":"Registers","d":"Cache Memory"},{"q":"Which register holds the memory address of the next instruction to be fetched?","a":"Instruction Register (IR)","b":"Program Counter (PC)","c":"Memory Address Register (MAR)","d":"Accumulator"},{"q":"Which type of cache memory is typically built directly into the CPU chip and is the fastest?","a":"L1 Cache","b":"L2 Cache","c":"L3 Cache","d":"System RAM"}]',
