  '["1011 in binary is (1*8) + (0*4) + (1*2) + (1*1) = 11.","In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15.","The Octal number system uses eight digits (0-7) and has base 8.","First-generation computers (1940-1956) used vacuum tubes for circuitry and magnetic drums for memory.","The ALU performs arithmetic calculations (addition, subtraction) and logical decisions.","The Program Counter (PC) stores the address of the next instruction in sequence to be executed.","L1 cache is the fastest and closest to the CPU core, built directly on-die.","Solid State Drives (SSDs) read and write data electronically to flash memory, avoiding mechanical latency.","The BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) initializes hardware components and boots the system bootstrap loader.","Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is the foundation of data communication on the World Wide Web.","DNS stands for Domain Name System. It resolves domain names to numerical IP addresses.","The HTTP 200 OK status code indicates that the request has succeeded.","SSL/TLS encrypts HTTP communications, rendering them secure under HTTPS.","IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses, whereas IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses, providing a massive address space.","Binary search cuts the search space in half with each iteration, giving logarithmic time complexity O(log n).","Big O notation describes the worst-case time complexity, providing an asymptotic upper bound.","Merge Sort is a divide-and-conquer algorithm with a guaranteed worst-case time complexity of O(n log n).","A Stack utilizes LIFO operations. Elements are added (pushed) and removed (popped) from the top.","Hash tables store key-value pairs using a hash function, allowing constant-time access on average.","Inheritance allows a subclass to reuse code and behaviors defined in a parent superclass.","Polymorphism allows a single interface or method to represent different underlying forms (e.g. method overriding).","Constructors initialize newly created 