d":"To compress hard drive data"},{"q":"Which protocol is responsible for transferring web pages from a server to a browser?","a":"FTP","b":"SMTP","c":"HTTP","d":"SSH"},{"q":"What does DNS stand for? (DBMS exam Focus)","a":"Domain Name System","b":"Data Network Service","c":"Digital Name Server","d":"Dynamic Node System"},{"q":"Which HTTP status code represents a successful resource retrieval?","a":"200 OK","b":"301 Moved Permanently","c":"404 Not Found","d":"500 Internal Server Error"},{"q":"Which protocol is used to securely encrypt the connection between a browser and a server?","a":"HTTP","b":"FTP","c":"SSL/TLS (HTTPS)","d":"Telnet"},{"q":"What is the primary difference between IPv4 and IPv6?","a":"IPv4 is 128-bit, IPv6 is 32-bit","b":"IPv4 is 32-bit, IPv6 is 128-bit","c":"IPv4 uses letters, IPv6 uses only numbers","d":"IPv4 is secure, IPv6 is not secure"},{"q":"What is the worst-case time complexity of a Binary Search algorithm?","a":"O(1)","b":"O(n)","c":"O(log n)","d":"O(n log n)"},{"q":"What notation is used to describe the upper bound of an algorithm''s execution time? (DBMS exam Focus)","a":"Omega Notation","b":"Theta Notation","c":"Big O Notation","d":"Alpha Notation"},{"q":"Which sorting algorithm splits an array in half, recursively sorts them, and merges them back?","a":"Bubble Sort","b":"Quick Sort","c":"Merge Sort","d":"Selection Sort"},{"q":"Which data structure follows the Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) access principle?","a":"Queue","b":"Stack","c":"Linked List","d":"Binary Tree"},{"q":"What is a major advantage of a Hash Table?","a":"It sorts elements automatically","b":"It provides average O(1) time complexity for search, insert, and delete operations","c":"It uses minimal memory","d":"It supports parent-child node relationships"},{"q":"Which OOP principle allows a class to inherit attributes and methods from another class?","a":"Encapsulation","b":"Inheritance","c":"Polymorphism","d":"Abstraction"},{"q":"What is Polymorphism? (DBMS exam Focus)","a":