  '["In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15.","1011 in binary is (1*8) + (0*4) + (1*2) + (1*1) = 11.","In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15.","The Octal number system uses eight digits (0-7) and has base 8.","First-generation computers (1940-1956) used vacuum tubes for circuitry and magnetic drums for memory.","The ALU performs arithmetic calculations (addition, subtraction) and logical decisions.","The Program Counter (PC) stores the address of the next instruction in sequence to be executed.","L1 cache is the fastest and closest to the CPU core, built directly on-die.","Solid State Drives (SSDs) read and write data electronically to flash memory, avoiding mechanical latency.","The BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) initializes hardware components and boots the system bootstrap loader.","Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is the foundation of data communication on the World Wide Web.","DNS stands for Domain Name System. It resolves domain names to numerical IP addresses.","The HTTP 200 OK status code indicates that the request has succeeded.","SSL/TLS encrypts HTTP communications, rendering them secure under HTTPS.","IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses, whereas IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses, providing a massive address space.","Binary search cuts the search space in half with each iteration, giving logarithmic time complexity O(log n).","Big O notation describes the worst-case time complexity, providing an asymptotic upper bound.","Merge Sort is a divide-and-conquer algorithm with a guaranteed worst-case time complexity of O(n log n).","A Stack utilizes LIFO operations. Elements are added (pushed) and removed (popped) from the top.","Hash tables store key-value pairs using a hash function, allowing constant-time access on average.","Inheritance allows a subclass to reuse code and behaviors defined in a parent superclass.","Polymorphism allows a single interface or method to represent different underlying forms (e.g. method overriding).","Constructors initialize newly created objects and are called automatically upon instantiation.","Exception handling (try-catch) intercepts errors at runtime, allowing graceful recovery.","The Heap is a large, unstructured pool of memory used for variables allocated dynamically at runtime.","Version Control Systems like Git track edits, support branching, and coordinate collaboration.","The Waterfall model is a rigid, step-by-step process where each phase must complete before the next begins.","Unit testing validates that small, isolated blocks of code (units) perform correctly.","White Box testing focuses on internal structures and requires access to the source code.","Ransomware locks or encrypts data, threatening to publish or delete it unless a ransom is paid.","Asymmetric encryption uses a public key to encrypt and a separate private key to decrypt.","Blockchain links cryptographic blocks in a distributed P2P consensus, guaranteeing immutability.","Securing easy points early ensures you don''''t run out of time for questions you definitely know.","Skipping questions you cannot eliminate options for prevents losing penalty points from negative marking.","1011 in binary is (1*8) + (0*4) + (1*2) + (1*1) = 11.","In hexadecimal, A represents 10, B is 11, C is 12, D is 13, E is 14, and F is 15.","The Octal number system uses eight digits (0-7) and has base 8.","First-generation computers (1940-1956) used vacuum tubes for circuitry and magnetic drums for memory.","The ALU performs arithmetic calculations (addition, subtraction) and logical decisions.","The Program Counter (PC) stores the address of the next instruction in sequence to be executed."]',
  'published',
  datetime('now', '+1576 hours')
);

