 (Use case diagram Focus)","a":"The ability of an object to take on multiple forms","b":"Hiding internal details using private attributes","c":"Bundling data and methods into a single class","d":"Running code in multiple threads"},{"q":"In OOP, what special function is automatically called when an object is instantiated?","a":"Destructor","b":"Constructor","c":"Getter","d":"Static method"},{"q":"What is exception handling?","a":"Finding syntax errors during compilation","b":"Managing runtime errors to prevent application crashes","c":"Optimizing database queries","d":"Using pointers to access heap memory"},{"q":"Which area of memory is used for dynamic memory allocation (e.g., malloc in C, new in C++)?","a":"Stack","b":"Heap","c":"Register","d":"Static Code Segment"},{"q":"Which tool allows developers to track and manage changes to source code over time?","a":"IDE","b":"Compiler","c":"Version Control System (e.g. Git)","d":"Debugger"},{"q":"Which SDLC model is characterized by sequential, non-overlapping phases? (Use case diagram Focus)","a":"Waterfall Model","b":"Agile Model","c":"Scrum Model","d":"Spiral Model"},{"q":"What testing level focuses on testing individual modules or functions in isolation?","a":"Integration Testing","b":"System Testing","c":"Unit Testing","d":"Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"Which testing type evaluates code structure, logic paths, and internal execution paths?","a":"Black Box Testing","b":"White Box Testing","c":"Gray Box Testing","d":"User Acceptance Testing"},{"q":"What is ransomware?","a":"A virus that copies email addresses","b":"Malware that encrypts files and demands payment to restore access","c":"Adware that redirects search engines","d":"A tool used to scan network ports"},{"q":"Which cryptographic method uses public and private keys for encryption and decryption?","a":"Symmetric Encryption","b":"Asymmetric Encryption","c":"Hashing","d":"Salting"},{"q":"What technology maintains a decentralized, immutable ledger of transactions? (U